      "id": 1,
      "text": "Leon was founded in 1832 when a slice of the old town of Conewango was carved out.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leon%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from Spain’s former Kingdom of León, though locals pronounce it “LEE-un.”.",
